<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate up, others mixed.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate up, others mixed.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	22.61	     +28	    22.59     22.68</p>
<p>91-Day	22.97		-1	    22.90     23.03</p>
<p>182-Day     22.99		 0	    22.90     23.09</p>
<p>350-Day     24.29				23.96     24.47</p>
<p>Last week the 357-day paper was assigned at 23.94 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   2.66 bln pesos    3.33</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   5.57 bln pesos    6.97</p>
<p>182-Day     800 million pesos   5.51 bln pesos    6.88</p>
<p>350-Day     600 million pesos   2.66 bln pesos    4.44</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 5.47 on demand of 16.40 billion pesos compared to 4.58 the week before on demand of 13.75 billion pesos the week before. Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			    7 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    6 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  10 basis points</p>
<p>    350-Day			  18 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
